      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PARTHENON (6) produced solid figures on debut when he took control from the outset to score over 1000m at Gosford. Claim helps again and has the upside to measure up again. ISAWYOU (1) bounced off his sound debut in town with a fighting victory over 1150m at Illawarra Grange. Faces a few hurdles today and can run into the minor money with the 3kg weight rise. TURF FEVER (3) lightly raced gelding resuming from a lengthy break. Showed ability in his first prep when winning on debut and placing at the provincials. Looks ready to go after the one 800m trial placing at Hawkesbury. Maps well and expected to go close. ROYAL CORPORAL (2) slow into stride first up and did plenty wrong in the run when last over 1300m at Kembla Grange. Blinkers come off and gets another chance from the rails draw.",
